From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 15:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server: on PS5, ask for a handle's in-process sync object on the client thread

With the in-process synchronization device on (patch 0890, WINE_PS5_NTSYNC=1) waits no longer reach
the server, but ntdll asks get_inproc_sync_fd for each handle it has not seen, and in a .NET game that
was about 375 requests a second at 16.5 us through the pipes, which kept the server time where it was
without the device. On the PS5 the handler looks the handle up, reads the object's device number
and takes a device reference for the client: no descriptor is passed (send_client_fd is the
non-PS5 branch), nothing sleeps, and the request carries a handle only. It joins the requests
patches 0918 and 0919 run on the calling thread.
---
  server/request.c | 3 +++
  1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/server/request.c b/server/request.c
index aea3463..c322de1 100644
--- a/server/request.c
+++ b/server/request.c
@@ -372,6 +372,9 @@ static int is_direct_request( enum request req )
     case REQ_remove_completion:
     case REQ_get_thread_completion:
     case REQ_query_completion:
+    /* the in-process device's number for a handle (patch 0890): a lookup and a
+     * device reference, no descriptor passed on the PS5 */
+    case REQ_get_inproc_sync_fd:
         return 1;
     default:
         return 0;
